  {
    "title_zh": "明星哪去了",
    "title_en": "Where Did the Star Go?",
    "target_age": "4-6",
    "source_type": "pdf",
    "source_file": "明星哪去了（4-6 岁）.pdf",
    "page_index_in_story": 3,
    "source_page": 3,
    "image_path": "images/slide_03.png",
    "page_text_ocr_zh": "给读者的话\n\n小朋友，你也喜欢白色啦，是不是？你看她，\n多么洁白、明净。可是，你想过吗，没有其他颜色\n的衬托，白色啦的洁白也就显不出来啦！\n这是为什么呢？请你拿一张白纸，再用一支白\n蜡笔，在纸上画个雪人。怎么样？画了半天，还是\n画不出来吧！可你再换上其他颜色的蜡笔，一会儿，\n一个有趣的雪人儿就画出来啦。\n白色啦成了明星，赶走了其他色啦朋友，结\n果，连她自己也不见了，白色啦为什么不见了？\n对！要用别的颜色来衬托，白色啦离不开其他\n色啦朋友。\n请你准备好红、橙、蓝、绿、紫几支\n彩笔，让我们一起来画白色啦，看谁把她\n画得更洁白，更可爱。",
    "page_text_en": "A Message to the Reader\n\nChild, you also like white, don't you? Look at her,\nhow pure and bright. But have you ever thought, without other colors\nfor contrast, the purity of white wouldn't show up!\nWhy is that? Take a white sheet of paper, then use a white\nwax crayon to draw a snowman on it. How does it go? After drawing for a while, you still\ncan't see it, right? But if you switch to other colored crayons, in no time,\na fun little snowman appears.\nWhite became the star, drove away other color friends, and as a result,\neven she herself disappeared. Why did white disappear?\nExactly! To show up, white needs other colors to contrast with. White can't do without her\nother color friends.\nPlease prepare a few colored pencils—red, orange, blue, green, purple—\nand let's draw white together. Let's see who can make her\neven purer and cuter.",
    "summary_zh": "本页是绘本的‘给读者的话’，通过提问和举例，向小读者解释白色需要其他颜色衬托才能显现其洁白，并邀请读者用彩色笔一起参与绘画，感受色彩的互动与美感。"
  },
